VRHS COUNSELING - GPA and Quartiles (text in an image on the page): Grade Point Average (GPA) and Rank in Class for Students Entering Grade 9 During the 2021-2022 School Year and Thereafter

At the December 17th, 2020 Leander ISD Board of Trustees meeting, changes to the Policy EIC (Local) were approved. This policy updated will change the method used to calculate weighted GPA and the reporting of class rank beginning with the class of 2025 (students entering grade nine in the 2021-2022 school year). The complete language to the change to Policy EIC (Local) can be found here, but significant changes are highlighted below.

Courses Included in the Calculation of Weighted GPA
A student’s weighted GPA will be used to calculate class rank. Courses included in the calculation of the weighted GPA will from the following areas:

1. Up to eight semesters in English/language arts;
2. Up to eight semesters in mathematics;
3. Up to eight semesters in science;
